{"data":[{"attachments":{"media_keys":["13_2109874368755183616"],"media_source_tweet_id":["2109874398656168211"]},"author_id":"1153194267138908160","created_at":"2026-10-13T18:11:02.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110070825269522481"],"id":"2110070825269522481","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":10,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"𝐇𝐚𝐫𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐯𝐩𝐮𝐫 41 Pally Club is one of South Kolkata’s most popular Durga Puja pandals. It is famous for its big, creative themes and attracts huge crowd. The 2026 theme reportedly explored “the different stages of life.\" https://t.co/FuqCWlUgFJ","url":"https://x.com/MonojitSinha11/status/2110070825269522481"},{"author_id":"3868003454","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:43:17.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109912846398271869"],"id":"2109912846398271869","note_tweet":{"text":"So there are some 3000 pandals in the city. Covering all of them won't be possible or practical. If you want to do just the big and famous one, even that would be some 200 pandals and on Ashtami/Navami visiting just one of them can eat up 5-6 hours. \n\nSo this needs planning. Divide the city geograpically. Fix your priorities. Maximize the usage of day hours when rush is relatively lesser. \n\nHere are few routes. \n\nFirst and foremost my top 2 routes for those visiting Kolkata just for experiencing Pujo. \n\n1. Old/North Kolkata Heritage Route: These are the OG pujos.\n\nBagbazar Sarbojanin → Ahiritola Sarbojanin → Kumartuli Park → Sovabazar Rajbari → Hatibagan Sarbojanin → Nalin Sarkar Street → Tala Prattoy.\n\n2. Kasba to Jodhpur Park - My go-to stretch. This is one of the longest stretch you can cover in one day covering 15+ famous ones if you are ready to do 50000 steps in a day. \n\nStart at Bosepukur Sitala Mandir → Bosepukur Talbagan → Ekdalia Evergreen → Singhi Park  → Deshapriya Park → Tridhara Sammilani → Hindustan Park → Maddox Square →Mudiali → Jodhpur Park\n\nThen there are routes to cover depending upon where you staying:\n\nSalt Lake Cluster: These have relatively lesser rush and can be easily covered within a few hours (unless you get stuck in FD block one which is largest in scale)\nFD Block → AK Block → BJ Block → BD Block (plus you visit any additional blocks on the route)\n\nBehala Cluster: Would recommend to visit these during night. Behala Club → Behala Buroshibtala Janakalyan Sangha → Behala Natun Dal → Barisha Club → Barisha Sarbojanin\n\nVIP Road Cluster: Telengabagan → Sreebhumi Sporting Club → Lake Town Association → Dum Dum Park Tarun Sangha → Bharat Chakra → Dum Dum Park Youth Association \n\nAlipore Cluster: Alipore Sarbojanin → Chetla Agrani → Badamtala Ashar Sangha → 66 Pally → Suruchi Sangha\n\nGaria Cluster: Naktala Udayan Sangha → Naktala Pally Unnayan Samity → Garia Naba Durga → Pancha Durga → Patuli Sarbojanin \n\nIf you are not from Kolkata, I would suggest avoid the big Pujas of Central Kolkata (Md. Ali Park → Santosh Mitra Square → College Square). They get insane crowd from people flocking Kolkata from nearby districts for a day due to nearness to Sealdah and Howrah stations. They are very popular but you need adventurous spirit to tackle them."},"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":53,"impression_count":3563,"like_count":91,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":4,"retweet_count":8},"text":"So there are some 3000 pandals in the city. Covering all of them won't be possible or practical. If you want to do just the big and famous one, even that would be some 200 pandals and on Ashtami/Navami visiting just one of them can eat up 5-6 hours. \n\nSo this needs planning. https://t.co/KYHxFmIMLJ","url":"https://x.com/EducatedMoron/status/2109912846398271869"},{"author_id":"740846832755052545","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:12:00.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109904974893474142"],"id":"2109904974893474142","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":85,"like_count":2,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"@Amit4Films @Parthib777 @Exoteric_savy I love pandal hopping but physically I’m not very capable. Also I can’t do the all nighter. But manage to see at least 20-30 pandal every year. Start with South. On Chaturthi. Suruchi, Ekdalia, Hindustan park, Tridhara, Deshopriya  and Ballygaunge cultural. the most famous ones.","url":"https://x.com/RitzyB94/status/2109904974893474142"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2109688073240100864"]},"author_id":"1341576373672898561","created_at":"2026-10-12T16:50:09.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109688083897827734"],"id":"2109688083897827734","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":11,"impression_count":2900,"like_count":409,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":5,"retweet_count":23},"text":"#4 Visited Barisha Club \n\nOne outstanding creation. https://t.co/ZfijTRPQVS","url":"https://x.com/SudhanidhiB/status/2109688083897827734"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2109349880020025344","3_2109349892980371456"]},"author_id":"1341576373672898561","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:26:21.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109349903600374159"],"id":"2109349903600374159","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":17,"impression_count":5953,"like_count":346,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":2,"retweet_count":27},"text":"#2 Visited Didi @keyakahe's Durga Puja at Rajdanga Naba Uday Sangha. Unreal colour combination as theme. https://t.co/bC8Dev0wKx","url":"https://x.com/SudhanidhiB/status/2109349903600374159"}],"includes":{"media":[{"height":1280,"media_key":"13_2109874368755183616","preview_image_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2109874368755183616/img/pnSwKmbN1UkvyPLx.jpg","type":"video","width":720},{"height":3873,"media_key":"3_2109688073240100864","type":"photo","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUceIABawAAKEur.jpg","width":3072},{"height":3230,"media_key":"3_2109349880020025344","type":"photo","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUXqikGbQAA--tN.jpg","width":2722},{"height":4000,"media_key":"3_2109349892980371456","type":"photo","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HU